prompt: Load the `writing-style` skill from ~/.claude/skills/writing-style/SKILL.md or ~/.kiro/steering/skills/writing-style/SKILL.md — whichever path exists, and follow its instructions for how to open a response that uses it. Then, in one short sentence, name the three things the skill lets me do with my prose. This fixture is the load/self-announce check for the writing-style set (a compliant agent emits the skill's own announce line without being told the literal text); the formatter and learning-loop fixtures verify the behavior.
expect_substr: [writing-style] applies
tools: claude,kiro,codex
